"""The TRUE-RANK determinantal object for D23 (rank-2 correction).

Facts established by det23_minors.py (x3 primes): A = C*diag(m) with
m = (uW1^2, uW2^2, uW1^2, uW2^2) and C a CONSTANT 6x4 matrix of rank 2;
hence all six 5x5 minors of [A|b] are the ZERO polynomial (vacuous),
and on the chart (uW_i = W_i^-1 != 0, enforced by the uW rows IN the
fiber ideal) rank A(x) = rank C = 2 EXACTLY at every fiber point.

Exact linear algebra over a field: with rank A(x) = 2 pinned,
  exists tg with A(x)tg = -b(x)
    <=> rank[A(x)|b(x)] = 2
    <=> u.b(x) = 0 for every u in leftker(C)  (4-dim, constant)
    <=> all 3x3 minors of [A(x)|b(x)] vanish.
leftker(C) contains the NF kernel vector a with a.b == 0 identically,
so the condition space {u.b : u in leftker(C)} is 3-dimensional:
THREE polynomials g1,g2,g3 (RREF-canonical basis) in the 22 fiber vars.

  V(fiberGB + g1,g2,g3) = proj_22 V(row22red)   (EQUIVALENCE, per-fiber
  scope: both directions, because rank A = 2 exactly on the chart).

This script: canonical leftker basis, the g rows, exact identities,
the full 200-strong 3x3 minor census (two routes on a sample), the
24-point kill-set evaluation of the g rows, cross-prime pattern gates.
Banked to det23_rank2.pkl for the emitter.
