+Hence `leftker(C)` has dimension four. One left-kernel vector annihilates the inhomogeneous term identically, and the other directions span exactly (g_1,g_2,g_3). Equivalently, the four preliminary eliminants (R_2,\ldots,R_5) have one exact constant syzygy and reduce to three conditions. That is the structural reason for “four becomes three”; it does **not** explain why three conditions have height only two on (V(I_{21})).
