+2. Rerun `gm_jet2`/`jrows` over dual numbers to obtain the exact \(A_{aqm},B_{aqm}\) in (O). Assert the 29 support starts above, the raw-label bijection below, `eta29 == 0`, and invariance under a second direct differentiation path.
+3. For each \(B_c\) and truncation \(N\), form the causal \(29N\times29N\) coefficient matrix \(M_c(N)\) from input coefficients \(u^0,\ldots,u^{N-1}\) to output coefficients of the same range. Put
+   \[
+   \delta_c(N)=29N-\operatorname{rank}M_c(N).
+   \]
+   Certify a bounded eventual defect \(d_c\) by a filtration-respecting recurrence/Ore-Popov calculation. Testing two or three values of \(N\) is insufficient: the diagonal blocks depend on the coefficient index modulo \(p\), so the certificate must cover a complete mod-\(p\) period or provide an exact Ore identity. Recurring resonance or unbounded defect means \(e_c=\infty\).
+4. For a finite block, compute the determinant-index analogue in global \(t\)-units:
+   \[
+   e_c=6d_c+\sum_a s_a-\sum_{q\in B_c}r_q
+       =6d_c+r_c-48.                                    \tag{V}
+   \]
+   Bank the rank profile and an explicit causal right inverse whose maximum filtration loss is at most \(e_c\). Formula (V) reduces to the sum of Smith exponents when the operator is genuinely \(R\)-linear; the right-inverse check is mandatory in the Ore case.
+5. Stop a block once a certified lower bound exceeds 11. The output certificate must contain the witness/deep-draw hash, free stream, all shifts, operator hash, period/Ore certificate, \(d_c,e_c\), right-inverse identity, and a replay proving \(D\mathcal E_s\) times that inverse to the claimed precision.
+
+The surplus bridge is now explicit. In the completed local differential algebra at \(s\), define
+
+\[
+ \widehat I_E=\overline{\bigl([u^j]H_a:0\le a\le28,\ j\ge0\bigr)}.
+\]
+
+Every raw source label must be mapped and checked as
+
+\[
+ (n,a)\longleftrightarrow
+ \left(a,\frac{n-s_a}{6}\right),
+\quad n\equiv s_a\pmod6,
+\]
