+**CONJECTURE K-D25:** if \(K\) is a genuine depth-ladder component rather than an accidental embedded component, the five Row-24 residuals should again have conormal rank well below five after reduction on each 11-dimensional survivor component. A bare 22-variable witness is insufficient: first treat the four dormant level-51 values and the remaining D23 lift-fiber coordinates symbolically over each base witness, form the five existential residuals, and measure their **projected** conormal rank after eliminating the reactivated variables; then repeat over each minimal component of \(G_{23}\). If the residual module descends to the 11-dimensional base (\(r=0\)), base-conormal rank 1–2 predicts a 9–10-dimensional D25 projection and rank 5 roughly dimension 6, still not generic emptiness. For \(r>0\), only the eliminated projected height supports a base-dimension prediction. A D25 kill would require an exceptional nonlinear incompatibility or unit ideal, not merely “five equations.”
